AUDIO: 'couldn\'t believe it was real. And in 24 hours, our&nbsp; life changed. At no point did I think I was going&nbsp;&nbsp; to come home with a Hobbit house. I learned&nbsp; what an escalating bid was. 10 years later,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'um, that is one little piece of the puzzle&nbsp; of how we ended up winning the 20-way bid.&nbsp;&nbsp; 356,000 [music] is what we paid. The home is just&nbsp; shy of 2400 square ft. It has a large living room,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'kitchen, dining room, a laundry room, and then&nbsp; two bedroom suites. Welcome to the Wisconsin&nbsp;&nbsp; Hobbit House. What you\'re looking at here, come&nbsp; with me, is two quanza huts. They\'ve been placed&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on grade. One is higher than the other. The&nbsp; lower quanzite hut is the living room, kitchen,&nbsp;&nbsp; and dining room. The upper both of the [music]&nbsp; bedroom suites. Would you like to come on in?'

