AUDIO: 'short ways, we\'ll be on the roof. So, here we are&nbsp; up on the roof and [music] one of the neat things&nbsp;&nbsp; is that this home is actually built into a bluff.&nbsp; Uh, the bluff right here is part of the drifless&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[09:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'region and that was a region of the Midwest that&nbsp; was spared by the glaciers and in turn is not&nbsp;&nbsp; uh as flat as the rest of the Great Plains. The&nbsp; Hobbit House has layer of soil and greenery all&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[09:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'over the top. Because we\'re part of this beautiful&nbsp; forest system, uh it\'s not uncommon for deer and&nbsp;&nbsp; other wildlife to find their way onto the top of&nbsp; the roof, and you do hear them from the inside. I designed the home to be a blank canvas. I didn\'t&nbsp; really entirely want to direct their experience&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[09:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here because I think there\'s people who are going&nbsp; to come here to find inspiration, to find peace,&nbsp;&nbsp; and to relax. But there may be people who&nbsp; are here to celebrate an anniversary and&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[10:10] [scene:talk]
